{"authored" [{"question" "q-24576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6} \\\\ y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{5}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{5} & =1-2{(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{y}{5} & =1-2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{5} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} \\\\ y & =-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6ff0a51ac75a21025e9d0e9a22eb512febb63f2fd44629e2b5f9555cf2074bb" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-18+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=1+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{6}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=5+{x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{5}-{x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fffa75881fdf84fcaa4c6090605923e526bf36a9fed64cd4ce6c8c12ac5a01" "basis" 1365 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039508/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-15759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a tangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "434bbc310bcc9fbc66abd7f8aa19f2097f08edade4492c2adb9bc6c8895259d7"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{2+{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6} \\\\ y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{5}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{5} & =1-2{(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{y}{5} & =1-2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{5} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} \\\\ y & =-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "434bbc310bcc9fbc66abd7f8aa19f2097f08edade4492c2adb9bc6c8895259d7"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-18+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}"] ["math" "y=-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}"] ["math" "y=1+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{6}"] ["math" "y=5+{x}^{2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{5}-{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-24576" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-5+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-276277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}+4,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-276277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=t+1\\,⇒\\,t=x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=x-1$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(x-1)^{2}+4 \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}-2x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is \n$y={x}^{2}-2x+5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-276277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "434bbc310bcc9fbc66abd7f8aa19f2097f08edade4492c2adb9bc6c8895259d7"} {"question" "q-276277" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-276277" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-1)^2+4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-9},\\,\\,\\,y=3{t}^{2},\\,t\\ge 3.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ge 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for ${t}^{2}:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-9}\\,⇒\\,{t}^{2}={x}^{2}+9\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${t}^{2}={x}^{2}+9$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=3({x}^{2}+9)=3{x}^{2}+27.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=3{x}^{2}+27.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 3$ and $x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-9},$ we must have $x\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is $y=3{x}^{2}+27,\\,x\\ge 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "434bbc310bcc9fbc66abd7f8aa19f2097f08edade4492c2adb9bc6c8895259d7"} {"question" "q-321090" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321090" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^2+27"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6} \\\\ y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{5}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{5} & =2{(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36})-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{36}-1 \\\\ y & =5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "434bbc310bcc9fbc66abd7f8aa19f2097f08edade4492c2adb9bc6c8895259d7"} {"question" "q-321318" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"} {"question" "q-321318" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5x^2}{18}-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2f4f905e4b44ce876243c987a8909c7e656867ae91f0dde9d64b2ea35ecc274"}] "usage" {"q-24576" []} "basis" 1922 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186302869 17592186302870 17592186302871 17592186302872 17592186302873] "immutable_fields" [[17592186302868 :answer-field/correct] [17592186302868 :answer-field/id] [17592186302868 :answer-field/key] [17592186302868 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
